course: dictionary
lesson: 5087
title: One word, two jobs: intellectual
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can work as more than one part of speech. Intellectual can be an adjective, which describes a thing, or a noun, which names a person. The words around it show you which one it is. Ask: what job is this word doing in the sentence?
explain: «She solved the puzzle with great intellectual skill.» Here intellectual describes the skill, so it is an adjective. It means about thinking, reasoning and understanding. Try the swap: «She solved the puzzle with great thinking skill» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: «Dad is an intellectual who reads about big ideas every night.» Here intellectual names a person, so it is a noun. The little word «an» before it is a clue, because it tells you a noun is coming. An intellectual is someone who thinks deeply and loves ideas, books and learning.
fact: Intellectual means about thinking, reasoning and understanding, as in «intellectual skills».
fact: As a noun, «an intellectual» is a person who thinks deeply and is interested in ideas, books and learning. The plural is «intellectuals».
fact: «Intellectual» can describe a film or book that asks you to think about serious ideas, as in «an intellectual film».
fact: «Intellectual property» means ideas and inventions that belong to someone.
fact: Other phrases with intellectual include «intellectual development» (how the mind grows) and «intellectual challenge» (a problem that makes you think hard).
exercise: «The puzzle gave the class an intellectual challenge.» What does intellectual mean here? | *About thinking and reasoning | Very loud | Made of paper | About running and jumping
exercise: «Maya is an intellectual who loves reading about big ideas.» In this sentence, what is an intellectual? | *A person who thinks deeply and loves ideas | A kind of sports game | A type of cold weather
exercise: «We watched an intellectual film about the meaning of time.» What does intellectual tell us about the film? | It is only for cartoons | It is in colour | *It is about serious ideas | It is very short
test: «Intellectual property» means ideas and inventions that belong to someone. Which of these is an example? | *An inventor's new design, owned by her | A cloud in the sky | Five apples on a plate | A puppy playing in a park
test: Ella says intellectual just means clever. What is a better explanation? | *Connected with thinking, reasoning and understanding | Connected with the weather | Connected with feeling and dancing | Connected with food and cooking
exam: In «She is a true intellectual», which word class is intellectual? | Adverb | Adjective | *Noun | Verb
